event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":330,"item_id":"fc_05ead64b871aca2a016adb622e0d1c8191ae37ce1a027c0f8f","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"source-order tensor action definition in interface header\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Continued API investigation and found the concrete cause of a previously unchecked interface defect: `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f` has type `(K ⊗[ℤ] M) →ₗ[K] (K ⊗[ℤ] M)`, not an endomorphism of `M ⊗[ℤ] K`. The source-order action must be implemented with a genuine K-linear map on M ⊗[ℤ] K (or explicit checked transport bridges ending in that carrier). A naive TensorProduct.map is only Z-linear and cannot be upgraded using an arbitrary Module K instance without proving the scalar compatibility. The current whole artifact is therefore not ready to submit as valid. This is formalization/API work, not a mathematical gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Actual check_lean_types output showing the lTensor domain and codomain in reversed tensor order; Mathlib `LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Tower.lean` lines 183-190 and 232-248 define map and lTensor, while 264-280 define rTensor. Source P requires the original M ⊗[ℤ] K order.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Corrected and typechecked the H004 proposition encoding; confirmed the nine top-level artifact keys pass using a minimal checker control; replaced vacuous plan ports with a single substantive exact-target obligation. The target action still needs a faithful Lean definition, and the full artifact has not passed structural/type checks or independent semantic review. No mathematical gap is established.\\\"}\"}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":331,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_05ead64b871aca2a016adb622e0d1c8191ae37ce1a027c0f8f","call_id":"call_99bfff7614c849c8bbddc1387152999d","name":"report_obstacle","arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"source-order tensor action definition in interface header\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Continued API investigation and found the concrete cause of a previously unchecked interface defect: `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f` has type `(K ⊗[ℤ] M) →ₗ[K] (K ⊗[ℤ] M)`, not an endomorphism of `M ⊗[ℤ] K`. The source-order action must be implemented with a genuine K-linear map on M ⊗[ℤ] K (or explicit checked transport bridges ending in that carrier). A naive TensorProduct.map is only Z-linear and cannot be upgraded using an arbitrary Module K instance without proving the scalar compatibility. The current whole artifact is therefore not ready to submit as valid. This is formalization/API work, not a mathematical gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Actual check_lean_types output showing the lTensor domain and codomain in reversed tensor order; Mathlib `LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Tower.lean` lines 183-190 and 232-248 define map and lTensor, while 264-280 define rTensor. Source P requires the original M ⊗[ℤ] K order.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Corrected and typechecked the H004 proposition encoding; confirmed the nine top-level artifact keys pass using a minimal checker control; replaced vacuous plan ports with a single substantive exact-target obligation. The target action still needs a faithful Lean definition, and the full artifact has not passed structural/type checks or independent semantic review. No mathematical gap is established.\\\"}\"}","status":"completed"}}

